# Files Nx must not see at all — neither when hashing a task nor when deciding
# what a commit affected.
#
# Why this exists on top of the `noMarkdown` named input in nx.json:
# `namedInputs` only control a task's *cache hash*. Affectedness is computed
# separately and is purely path-based — Nx marks a project affected when any
# file under its root changed, whatever the target's inputs say. CI has no
# shared Nx cache (no Nx Cloud, no cache action), so on a cold runner a
# markdown-only commit would still schedule and really run every build and
# test. Only `.nxignore` removes those files from the touched-file set, and
# with it the tasks disappear instead of being replayed.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow: `packages/*` markdown is documentation and
# nothing else. tsup builds from `src/`, vitest synthesises its own fixtures
# into temp dirs, and no package reads a checked-in `.md` at build or test
# time. Root markdown (AGENTS.md, README.md, ...) already affects nothing —
# it belongs to no project root and is not in `sharedGlobals`.
#
# NOT ignored, on purpose:
#   - apps/strauss-kb-docs/**  — the Docusaurus site's markdown IS its source.
#   - plugins/**               — a plugin's commands and skills are markdown,
#                                and that markdown is what it ships.
# Anything added later that compiles, tests or publishes markdown must stay
# out of this list too.
packages/**/*.md
